      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining OAuth Flow**\n\nI'm working on the `start_oauth_login.py` script. The primary focus right now is to set up a login flow. I've chosen Google as the OAuth provider. The next step is to select the authorization code grant flow as the login method.\n\n\n**Constructing Authorization URL**\n\nI'm now focusing on constructing the Google authorization URL. I've laid out the foundation by importing `os` to fetch credentials. I'm moving toward defining the Google-specific constants and retrieving the environment variables. The plan is to create a function, `start_google_oauth_login`, which will assemble the URL, including the crucial parameters. I'm paying attention to the `client_id`, `redirect_uri`, scope, `response_type`, and `access_type` parameters. The function will return the constructed authorization URL.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789860389018,
          "start": 1789860386381
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bbfe164d001jXHUZWRKiNOXu3",
